From 7a8a7ac8d1f2fe6261330470b46dde7f3c4590f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 17:17:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(seasonal): plug effective interval into next_due_at
 recalculation (#67, 2/3)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wires SeasonalIntervalService into every place that recomputes
next_due_at from an interval, so the seasonal correction takes effect
without changing any user-visible interval. No bulk migration of
existing next_due_at values — per AC, only future calculations use the
new interval; existing scheduled-but-not-yet-fired notifications are
left alone.

CareSchedule (domain):
  - rescheduleFrom(from) is unchanged in semantics — still applies
    intervalDays. New overload rescheduleFrom(from, intervalOverride)
    accepts an explicit interval. The entity stays unaware of
    SeasonalIntervalService — that's a service-layer concern.

Integration points (5 total):
  1. NotificationCallbackService.markScheduleDone — the «✅ Полил»
     button on a notification (generic path for all task types).
     Reads user from plant.getUser(), computes effective interval,
     uses the new rescheduleFrom overload.
  2. NotificationCallbackService — «watering with details» path
     (the soil-check + abundance flow, issue #71). Same treatment.
  3. NotificationSchedulerService.sendOneSchedule — admin-trigger /
     forced resend uses effective interval for advancement.
  4. NotificationSchedulerService.skipOneSchedule — the «⏭ Пропустить»
     action. Now correctly skips by the seasonal interval, not the
     raw base. Otherwise a winter «skip» would advance by 10 days
     when the active interval is 12.
  5. PlantService.toggleSchedule — both branches:
       - reactivating a stale schedule (next_due_at in the past) →
         recomputes with effective interval
       - creating a fresh schedule with the default → uses effective.
  6. PlantTemplateService.createPlantFromTemplate — both watering
     and the secondary schedules (MISTING/FERTILIZING). Uses a probe
     Plant with INHERIT override since the real Plant doesn't exist
     yet at that point.

Deliberately NOT touched:
  - PlantService.updateScheduleInterval: changing the base interval
    does NOT shift the existing next_due_at. The user is expected to
    re-schedule manually if they want an immediate shift. The AC
    «фактический интервал должен обновиться сразу» is still met:
    the *next* «полил» will apply the new base × current season.
  - NotificationCallbackService snooze handlers (lines 175/856/865/909):
    these are user-explicit «отложить на N дней» actions — applying
    seasonality would override what the user just chose.
  - All admin and projection paths (CalendarService) — they don't
    write next_due_at, only project it; seasonal is per-cycle, not
    per-projection.

No new tests in this commit — the integration is mechanical (call
effectiveIntervalDays, pass result into rescheduleFrom), and the
service's behavior is already covered by SeasonalIntervalServiceTest
in commit 1/3. The UI layer in commit 3/3 will add more test surface.
